.TH OMX-COMPLEMENT-SYNC 1 "2026-10-28" "omx-panel" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omx-complement-sync \- give the inferred port groups to every LV2 plugin that lacks them
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omx-complement-sync
.RB [ --dry-run ]
.RB [ --verbose ]
.br
.B omx-complement-sync
.B --check
.SH DESCRIPTION
For each installed LV2 bundle on the LV2 search list holding a plugin whose port groups
.B omx-panel complement
infers with confidence, writes a bundle named omx-complement-<bundle>.lv2 in MODGUI_DIR. It restates every TTL file lilv reads for the installed bundle, statement for statement, keeps lv2:binary pointing at the installed library, raises each plugin's lv2:microVersion by one (lv2:minorVersion unchanged), and adds the group nodes (lv2:symbol, lv2:name, lv2:displayPriority) and pg:group on each grouped port. lilv then loads it in place of the installed bundle. Every other file of the installed bundle is linked in, so a plugin that reads its own files finds them.
.PP
The installed bundle is never touched. Deleting the written bundle is the whole removal: lilv loads the installed one again.
.PP
Nothing is written for a bundle none of whose plugins needs groups: a plugin that carries its own, fits one screen of four, or has no confident grouping is left exactly as it is.
.PP
A bundle whose marker file .omx-complement-sync names the same installed bundle, the same content hash and the same writer is left as it is; one whose installed files or rules changed is written again. A bundle of that name without the marker is never written.
.PP
A bundle of ours no longer wanted is removed, one line naming it and why: its installed bundle is gone (the package was removed) or no longer on the search list, changed into one that is refused or declares no plugin, or none of its plugins comes out grouped on the current rules. lilv then loads the installed bundle again. Only a directory named omx-complement-*.lv2 holding the marker is ever removed; a directory without the marker, of another name, or a symbolic link is left alone.
.PP
A bundle the restatement cannot carry is refused, named with its reason, and never fails the run: TTL the reader cannot parse, a version that is not an integer or is at lilv's ceiling, more than one version or binary for a plugin, a plugin declared in more than one installed bundle, a dynamic manifest, a data file outside the bundle, a generated group node whose IRI the bundle already states or that two of its plugins would share (group-iri-collision).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --dry-run
say what would be written and removed, and change nothing
.TP
.B --verbose
also print each plugin's verdict: grouped (with its groups), nothing to do or no confident grouping (with the reason)
.TP
.B --check
change nothing and report: the LV2 search list and where it came from, whether MODGUI_DIR is on it, whether the LV2_PATH that the mod-host and mod-ui units run with holds MODGUI_DIR, and each bundle of ours that is stale (a sync removes it) or out of date (a sync writes it again); a bundle not written yet is named missing and is not stale
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LV2_PATH
the LV2 search list. Unset, it is plugin-hostd's default: /usr/lib64/lv2:/usr/lib/lv2:/usr/local/lib/lv2
.TP
.B MODGUI_DIR
the bundles, omx-modgui-sync's directory (default /usr/local/lib/lv2 for root, ~/.lv2 for a user). It must be on the LV2_PATH the plugin hosts read
.TP
.B STATE_DIR
the work files, omx-modgui-sync's (default /var/lib/omx/modgui-sync; $XDG_DATA_HOME/omx/modgui-sync for a user other than root)
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/omx/modgui-sync.conf
KEY=value lines for the variables above, read by the unit, shared with omx-modgui-sync
.TP
.I omx-complement-sync.service
runs the sync once; installed but not enabled (systemctl enable omx-complement-sync). Enabled, it runs at boot and each time plugin-qualify-sync finishes (a drop-in, plugin-qualify-sync.service.d/omx-complement-sync.conf, queues it from ExecStartPost when the unit is enabled); plugin-qualify's package triggers start that scan once per package transaction in the standard LV2 folders, so an install, upgrade or removal is followed by this run.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
the run finished, whatever it refused or removed; or --check found no bundle of ours stale or out of date
.TP
.B 1
the run could not start (omx-panel missing, MODGUI_DIR not writable); or --check could not read the bundles
.TP
.B 2
usage error
.TP
.B 3
--check only: at least one bundle of ours is stale (a sync removes it) or out of date (a sync writes it again), each named on its own line
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR omx-modgui-sync (1),
.BR omx-panel (1)
